# govulncheck findings that scripts/govulncheck.sh leaves out of its output.
#
# One entry per line: the ID, then why it is safe to leave out. An entry
# only hides a finding the code does not call (found in a required module
# or an imported package). If the code ever calls the vulnerable symbol,
# the finding is reported and the check fails, listed here or not. The
# script names an entry that no longer matches any finding, so it can be
# removed.

GO-2026-5932  golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained (no fix will come). The proxy imports nothing from openpgp; the module is required for other x/crypto packages. Listed 2026-10-27.
